"Let $H\\colon\\Omega\\times\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}_{\\geq 0}$ be a symmetric measurable weighted graph, or model. Call $H$ **clique-maximizing** if cliques maximize the relevant homomorphism quantity among the graph class under consideration. **Converse clique-maximizing conjecture.** If $H$ is clique-maximizing, then $H$ is ferromagnetic, equivalently positive semidefinite. The paper proves that every ferromagnetic model is clique-maximizing, so this conjecture asks for the converse characterization; the supplied text states that the converse is false."